  "articleBody": "Swapping old counters for fresh surfaces sounds straightforward, but old adhesives, stubborn fasteners, and settled walls can complicate the job. Understanding how to handle removal protects your existing cabinets from structural damage.\n\nWhat Can Change the Right Choice\n\nOld laminate or tile counters are often glued and screwed firmly into cabinet face frames. Forcing them off can split face rails, crack drawer slides, or pull cabinet boxes away from drywall. Your plan must account for whether existing backsplashes are staying or going. Removing an old deck often tears drywall paper behind it or chips lower backsplash tiles. Furthermore, once old tops are lifted, you may discover out-of-level frames, sagging corners, or hidden water damage around the sink base that requires carpentry repair before new surfaces can go down.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\n\nHaving an experienced finish contractor on site is crucial when replacing tops over older cabinetry. A general contractor can carefully cut adhesive seams, shim and reinforce base units, address damaged drywall, and coordinate the plumbing disconnects and reconnects under the sink. This multi-trade approach keeps your kitchen functional without unnecessary cabinet replacement costs.\n\nReady to upgrade your surfaces? Call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to review your kitchen countertop replacement plan.",
